(part with holes, cut inside-first)
(PureCutCNC reference program for the QtPlasmaC simulator check, issue #954.)
(Hand-written from the QtPlasmaC manual for LinuxCNC 2.9; each stanza names)
(the manual section it comes from. See ../README.md.)

(Manual: Preamble and Postamble Codes)
G21 G40 G49 G64 P0.1 G80 G90 G92.1 G94 G97
(Manual: Paused Motion)
M52 P1
(Manual: Automatic Material Handling - select, wait, then take the feed rate)
(from the material; the three codes must come in this order)
M190 P1
M66 P3 L3 Q1
F#<_hal[plasmac.cut-feed-rate]>

(Holes before the outline: once the outline is cut the part is loose on the)
(slats, so anything inside it has to be finished first.)

(hole 1: 40 mm, centre X55 Y60, counter-clockwise, pierced at the centre)
G0 X55 Y60
M3 $0 S1
G1 X75 Y60
G3 X75 Y60 I-20 J0
M5 $0

(hole 2: 40 mm, centre X105 Y60)
G0 X105 Y60
M3 $0 S1
G1 X125 Y60
G3 X125 Y60 I-20 J0
M5 $0

(outline: 120 x 80 plate, clockwise, pierced 5 mm outside the part)
G0 X15 Y60
M3 $0 S1
G1 X20 Y60
G1 X20 Y100
G1 X140 Y100
G1 X140 Y20
G1 X20 Y20
G1 X20 Y60
M5 $0

(Manual: Preamble and Postamble Codes)
G0 X0 Y0
G21 G40 G49 G64 P0.1 G80 G90 G92.1 G94 G97
M2
